# The compiled CSS, JS and fonts are COMMITTED, deliberately.
#
# Normally these are built on the machine that deploys. These installs land on
# shared cPanel hosting with no terminal and no Node, so there is nowhere to
# run `npm run build` at the far end — the assets have to arrive with the code
# or they do not arrive at all. Committing them makes `git pull` a complete
# deploy instead of a pull plus a manual upload that is easy to forget.
#
# The cost is real and accepted: every asset change writes ~1.1 MB of new
# binaries into the history, and whoever changes anything under resources/ must
# run `npm run build` and commit the result in the same commit. A stale build
# committed is worse than none — the shop would serve last week's stylesheet
# against this week's markup. AssetBuildTest is what catches that.
#
# /public/build is NOT ignored.
#
# An ARCHIVE of it is a different matter. `public/build.zip` was committed on
# 2026-09-09 — one day after the folder itself started being tracked, so it was
# already redundant when it arrived — and it sat there unreferenced: nothing in
# the code, the docs or CI mentioned it, and `shop:provision` copies the folder,
# never the zip. 0.7 MB in every clone and every pull, and a second copy of the
# assets that can silently fall out of step with the first. Removed 2026-09-12,
# and ignored so it cannot come back by hand.
/public/build.zip
/public/build.tar.gz
/public/fonts-manifest.dev.json
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
